        {
          "_comment": "Cone constant n = log(cos φ₁ / cos φ₂) / log( tan(π/4+φ₂/2) / tan(π/4+φ₁/2) ) (Appendix B). Depends only on the two standard parallels, so it differs between the WRF (≈0.7156) and NEI2016 (≈0.6305) parameter sets — this is what makes the rule genuinely parameterized rather than hard-coded.",
          "lhs": "n",
          "rhs": {
