                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "cos",
                        "args": [
                          "phi1"
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "cos",
                        "args": [
                          "phi2"
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "log",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      "t2",
                      "t1"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "Scale factor F = cos φ₁ · tan(π/4+φ₁/2)^n / n (Appendix B). The constant that ties the cone to the sphere; combined with R it sets every radius.",
          "lhs": "F",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "cos",
                    "args": [
                      "phi1"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "^",
                    "args": [
                      "t1",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "n"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "R·F — the radius scale in metres (R is the sphere radius). A convenience observed: ρ, ρ₀ and the inverse latitude all read R·F, so naming it keeps those three simple.",
          "lhs": "RF",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "R",
              "F"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "ρ₀ = R·F / tan(π/4+φ₀/2)^n (Appendix B). Radius from the cone apex to the origin parallel; the y-axis is measured down from here.",
          "lhs": "rho0",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              "RF",
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  "t0",
                  "n"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "ρ = R·F / tan(π/4+φ/2)^n (Appendix B). Radius from the cone apex to the input latitude.",
          "lhs": "rho",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              "RF",
              {
                "op": "^",
                "args": [
                  "tphi",
                  "n"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "θ = n·(λ−λ₀), the polar angle on the cone, with the longitude difference (lon−lon_0) converted to radians. Appendix B writes x = ρ·sin(n(λ−λ₀)).",
          "lhs": "theta",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "n",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "lon",
                      "lon_0"
                    ]
                  },
                  "deg2rad"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "FORWARD map, easting (metres): x = ρ·sin θ (Appendix B). At lon=lon_0, θ=0 ⇒ x=0 (the central meridian is the y-axis).",
          "lhs": "proj_x",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "rho",
              {
                "op": "sin",
                "args": [
                  "theta"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "FORWARD map, northing (metres): y = ρ₀ − ρ·cos θ (Appendix B). At (lon_0,lat_0): θ=0 and ρ=ρ₀ ⇒ y=0 (the projection origin maps to the false origin (0,0)).",
          "lhs": "proj_y",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "rho0",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "rho",
                  {
                    "op": "cos",
                    "args": [
                      "theta"
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "ρ₀ − y, the northing measured up from the cone apex. Composes on the FORWARD observed proj_y, so the inverse∘forward is the identity BY CONSTRUCTION (the longlat precedent: the inverse reads the forward observeds). Equals ρ·cos θ. Used by both ρ (inverse) and θ (inverse).",
          "lhs": "rho0_my",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "-",
            "args": [
              "rho0",
              "proj_y"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "INVERSE: ρ = sign(n)·sqrt(x² + (ρ₀−y)²) (Appendix B). Recovers the radius from the projected point; sign(n) keeps ρ on the correct side for either hemisphere's cone. For the round-trip this equals the forward ρ.",
          "lhs": "rho_inv",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "sign",
                "args": [
                  "n"
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "sqrt",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      {
                        "op": "^",
                        "args": [
                          "proj_x",
                          2.0
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "op": "^",
                        "args": [
                          "rho0_my",
                          2.0
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "INVERSE: θ = atan2(x, ρ₀−y) (Appendix B). Recovers the polar angle; atan2(ρ sinθ, ρ cosθ)=θ for ρ>0, so it inverts the forward θ.",
          "lhs": "theta_inv",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "atan2",
            "args": [
              "proj_x",
              "rho0_my"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "INVERSE longitude (degrees): λ = λ₀ + θ/n, converted back to degrees: geo_lon = lon_0 + (θ_inv/n)·(180/π). inverse∘forward = lon_0 + (n(lon−lon_0))/n = lon — the round-trip identity the acceptance checks.",
          "lhs": "geo_lon",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              "lon_0",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      "theta_inv",
                      "n"
                    ]
                  },
                  "rad2deg"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "INVERSE latitude (degrees): φ = 2·atan( (R·F/ρ)^(1/n) ) − π/2 (Appendix B), converted to degrees. Since R·F/ρ = tan(π/4+φ/2)^n, this returns the input latitude: inverse∘forward = φ. The round-trip identity in latitude.",
          "lhs": "geo_lat",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "-",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "*",
                    "args": [
                      2.0,
                      {
                        "op": "atan",
                        "args": [
                          {
                            "op": "^",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "/",
                                "args": [
                                  "RF",
                                  "rho_inv"
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "/",
                                "args": [
                                  1.0,
                                  "n"
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "/",
                    "args": [
                      3.141592653589793,
                      2.0
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              "rad2deg"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "_comment": "SURFACING state for the forward easting: d(forward_x)/dt = proj_x from a zero IC ⇒ du = x. Lets the gate read the forward output and compare to the proj4 reference points.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "forward_x"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "proj_x"
        },
        {
          "_comment": "SURFACING state for the forward northing: d(forward_y)/dt = proj_y ⇒ du = y.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "forward_y"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "proj_y"
        },
        {
          "_comment": "SURFACING state for the inverse∘forward longitude: d(roundtrip_lon)/dt = geo_lon ⇒ du = lon_0 + (n(lon−lon_0))/n = lon. Acceptance: roundtrip_lon == lon.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "roundtrip_lon"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "geo_lon"
        },
        {
          "_comment": "SURFACING state for the inverse∘forward latitude: d(roundtrip_lat)/dt = geo_lat ⇒ du = lat. Acceptance: roundtrip_lat == lat.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "roundtrip_lat"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": "geo_lat"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
